{"name":"Whipped Coconut Cream","hex":"#edece7","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"whipped","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of food: prepared by whipping or beating.","Ellipsis of pussywhipped."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["simple past and past participle of whip"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/whipped"},{"term":"coconut","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A fruit of the coconut palm (not a true nut), Cocos nucifera, having a fibrous husk surrounding a large seed.","A hard-shelled seed of this fruit, having white flesh and a fluid-filled central cavity."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/coconut"},{"term":"cream","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The butterfat or milkfat part of milk which rises to the top; this part when separated from the remainder.","The liquid separated from milk, possibly with certain other milk products added, and with at least eighteen percent of it milkfat."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Cream-coloured; having a yellowish white colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cream"}],"entries":[{"title":"Coconut cream","blocks":[{"text":"Coconut cream is similar to coconut milk, but is thicker due to a higher concentration of coconut and a lower amount of water in a ratio of about 4:1. Coconut cream is used as an ingredient in cooking, and has an unsweetened flavor."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/20/Coconut_cream_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Coconut_cream_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Coconut_cream","wikidata":"Q1139302"},{"title":"Coconut","blocks":[{"text":"The coconut is a member of the palm family (Arecaceae) and the only living species of the genus Cocos. The term \"coconut\" can denote the whole coconut palm tree or the large hard fruit. Originally native to the Southeast Asia, New Guinea, and the Southwestern Pacific, they are ubiquitous in coastal tropical regions."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/32/Cocos_nucifera_-_K%C3%B6hler%E2%80%93s_Medizinal-Pflanzen-187.jpg/330px-Cocos_nucifera_-_K%C3%B6hler%E2%80%93s_Medizinal-Pflanzen-187.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Coconut","wikidata":"Q3342808"},{"title":"Cream","blocks":[{"text":"Cream is a dairy product composed of the higher-fat layer skimmed from the top of milk before homogenization. The butterfat, which is less dense, rises to the top and is skimmed off, resulting in gravity cream. The industrial production of cream instead uses centrifugal separators to make separator cream. Cream is often sold in grades defined by their butterfat content. It contains high levels of saturated fat, in ascending proportion from light cream to heavy cream."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f7/01_Mmm..._Apple_Crisp_with_Whipped_Cream.jpg/330px-01_Mmm..._Apple_Crisp_with_Whipped_Cream.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cream","wikidata":"Q13228"},{"title":"Cream (colour)","blocks":[{"text":"Cream is the color of the cream produced by cattle grazing on natural pasture with plants rich in yellow carotenoid pigments, some of which are incorporated into the fresh milk. This gives a yellow tone to otherwise-white milk at higher fat concentrations. Cream is the pastel colour of yellow, much as pink is to red. By mixing yellow and white, cream can be produced."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ec/Milk_heavy_cream_B.jpg/330px-Milk_heavy_cream_B.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cream_(colour)","wikidata":"Q2730433"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d4/Coco3wjf.JPG/